exit 1

Date on this file: 2026-08-16
Running on Ubuntu Server 26.04, with MySQL v8.4 (v9 exists)

Basic tasks
    Install mysql-server: sudo apt-get --yes update && sudo apt-get install --yes mysql-server
    Check that it's running: sudo systemctl status mysql
    Open the TCP port 3306: sudo ufw allow MySQL
    Initialize security: sudo mysql_secure_installation
        Would you like to setup VALIDATE PASSWORD component? Y
        Please enter 0 = LOW, 1 = MEDIUM and 2 = STRONG: 2
        Change the password for admin ? Y
        New password: [Get from 1Password]
        Do you wish to continue with the password provided? Y
        Remove anonymous users? Y
        Disallow root login remotely? Y
        Remove test database and access to it? Y
        Reload privilege tables now? Y
    NOT DONE HERE: Neither root nor lhensley are defined. Yet.
        For root, use sudo and no password: sudo mysql -u root
            THEN set the password with this SQL: ALTER USER 'root'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY 'root-password';
                    # get 'root-password' from 1Password
                exit; # If you're done
        For lhensley: use this: mysql # (No sudo)
            THEN set the password with this SQL: CREATE USER 'lhensley'@'%' IDENTIFIED BY 'lhensley-password';
                    # get 'lhensley-password' from 1Password
            THEN set the permissions for lhensley with this SQL:
                GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, CREATE, DROP, RELOAD, SHUTDOWN, PROCESS, FILE, REFERENCES, 
                    INDEX, ALTER, SHOW DATABASES, SUPER, CREATE TEMPORARY TABLES, LOCK TABLES, EXECUTE, 
                    REPLICATION SLAVE, REPLICATION CLIENT, CREATE VIEW, SHOW VIEW, CREATE ROUTINE, ALTER ROUTINE, 
                    CREATE USER, EVENT, TRIGGER, CREATE TABLESPACE, CREATE ROLE, DROP ROLE ON *.* 
                    TO `lhensley`@`%` WITH GRANT OPTION;
                GRANT ALLOW_NONEXISTENT_DEFINER,APPLICATION_PASSWORD_ADMIN,AUDIT_ABORT_EXEMPT,AUDIT_ADMIN,
                    AUTHENTICATION_POLICY_ADMIN,BACKUP_ADMIN,BINLOG_ADMIN,BINLOG_ENCRYPTION_ADMIN,CLONE_ADMIN,
                    CONNECTION_ADMIN,ENCRYPTION_KEY_ADMIN,FIREWALL_EXEMPT,FLUSH_OPTIMIZER_COSTS,FLUSH_PRIVILEGES,
                    FLUSH_STATUS,FLUSH_TABLES,FLUSH_USER_RESOURCES,GROUP_REPLICATION_ADMIN,
                    GROUP_REPLICATION_STREAM,INNODB_REDO_LOG_ARCHIVE,INNODB_REDO_LOG_ENABLE,OPTIMIZE_LOCAL_TABLE,
                    PASSWORDLESS_USER_ADMIN,PERSIST_RO_VARIABLES_ADMIN,REPLICATION_APPLIER,
                    REPLICATION_SLAVE_ADMIN,RESOURCE_GROUP_ADMIN,RESOURCE_GROUP_USER,ROLE_ADMIN,
                    SENSITIVE_VARIABLES_OBSERVER,SERVICE_CONNECTION_ADMIN,SESSION_VARIABLES_ADMIN,SET_ANY_DEFINER,
                    SHOW_ROUTINE,SYSTEM_USER,SYSTEM_VARIABLES_ADMIN,TABLE_ENCRYPTION_ADMIN,TELEMETRY_LOG_ADMIN,
                    TRANSACTION_GTID_TAG,XA_RECOVER_ADMIN ON *.* TO `lhensley`@`%` WITH GRANT OPTION;
                FLUSH PRIVILEGES;
            Update the passwords in ~/.my.cnf and in /root.
        CONSIDER: Stop using lhensley in normal use, and use admin. They have the same privileges.
    Restore any dump/backup applicable. EXAMPLE CLI COMMAND BELOW, you'll need to adjust this to your circumstances.
        sudo cp /mnt/4TBA/lifeboat/backups/2026-08-14-dsm1.sql /home/lhensley/
        sudo chown lhensley:lhensley /home/lhensley/2026-08-14-dsm1.sql
        sudo mysql --force -u root < /home/lhensley/2026-08-14-dsm1.sql # THIS WILL TAKE A LONG TIME.  2:15:40
        sudo rm /home/lhensley/2026-08-14-dsm1.sql

